      {
        "review_id": 232984253,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r232984253-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Namaste",
        "text": "The cremation ghats along the river Bagmati are used for open-air public cremations, which take place daily on the south bank. I was told that only royals and higher castes can be cremated directly in front of the temple. For a hefty NRs1000, non-Hindus can enter the compound and witness the open-air cremations. Witnessing the ceremony form the very beginning up to the end was an immensely poignant experience. If you do want to visit here and witness this spitriual and very personal ritual, carry with you some tact and respect and avoid taking pictures or videos as some tourists/foreigners were doing. The sad part was that some of the people who work for the temple secretly allow tourists closer to the viewing cremation deck and let them take pictures or videos for a little dollar amount. I was summoned a couple of times, but I politely declined the offer. Just sit from across the river and ruminate on in the experience, a surge of peaceful sentiment will come to you right away. Namaste!",
        "review_tip": null,
