        "title": "Temple?",
        "text": "The cost of the entrance (around 10$) gave me huge expectations. A local guide asking me for 10$ to show me the whole area made me believe that the place is huge an amazing... but it is not. I mean, in terms of religion and tradition, the place has a very strong humanity inside, but in architectural or artistic terms, is not that amazing, also because the most amazing part is reserved for Hindu people.\nThe place is crowded and I felt uncomfortable about having many people around looking at the cremation piles as it was a show...\nWould only recommend this place if you are looking for a deep human experience, but not just for fun",
