      {
        "review_id": 231567702,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r231567702-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "For something more serious...",
        "text": "Being able to go and visit this temple is a huge privilege. The temple itself is beautiful, but know that this is where any people that have passed on are brought to be burned. This is tradition in Nepali culture. I was able to sit on the opposite side of the river bank and take it all in, but it was very emotional as the families of these people mourned. Be respectful, quiet, and make sure to be mindful as you might be sitting next to a family member like I was. I didn't speak her language, but as I had tears streaming down my face, I looked at her and touched her arm to offer my condolences. \n\nThis place also has monkeys! Watch out! ",
