        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r231030244-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Outstanding place to visit but see the warnings",
        "text": "This is a magical place but 2 health warnings\n\na) Families need to be aware that bodies are cremated here and you may see this up close\nb) Monkeys are frequent and can be very aggressive so be aware with young children.\n\nThis is an extensive temple complex and it can be quite baffling if you come in at one of the unfamiliar entrances. You cant get into the Hindu Temple but walk around the side, go across the bridge and walk through the Ghats, up the steps to the temple complexes and just see how water, spirits and people come together. You can easily spend hours here - walking ,sitting, watching but its usually busy so be respectful and see how the spirit world is alive and well. Outstanding\n\n",
