      {
        "review_id": 230624397,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r230624397-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "Peace and complete satisfaction",
        "text": "Only Hindu's are allowed inside the temple premises. Probably this was my Nth visit to Lord Pashupati since I travel very frequently to Nepal and whenever I come to Nepal I always go for the darshan at least once every visit. As always - you get peace and complete satisfaction once you get the darshan. If you go around 10 am - all the 4 doors are opened and you get less crowd and darshan at ease. The temple opens at 4:30 am and till around 10 am, only the West door is open from which darshan is available which becomes crowded at times. If you go around 10 am, you can get the darshan at ease from any other doors which are all opened and even do Abishek at leisure. Remember, the temple closes around 12:30 noon and reopens at around 5:30 pm, so plan your Kathmandu sight seeing accordingly.",
