      {
        "review_id": 230471745,
        "review_link": "https://www.tripadvisor.com/ShowUserReviews-g293890-d310712-r230471745-Pashupatinath_Temple-Kathmandu_Kathmandu_Valley_Bagmati_Zone_Central_Region.html",
        "title": "The temple of Lord of the Beings...!",
        "text": "\"Pashu\" means living beings. So Pashpathinath literally means \"Lord of the beings\". As per Hinduism Lord Shiva is regarded as the father of all beings and so he is the Lord of all beings. Thus Pashupatinath is one of the important name for God Shiva.\nThe Inner temple well renowned for aged old sacredness. For the \"Shiva Ratri \" Festival Hundreds of thousand devotees visit this place, including devotees from India. Nepal President and Prime  minister  also visit the place for to respect the temple, on this day.\nThe river \"Bagumati\" is regarded as sacred as the river Ganges, in India.Many of the Hindu funeral rituals were done here. Dead bodies wrapped in suitable clothing, burned to ashes on the bank . Then the ashes will be floated in the river water.\nThe main temple, which is keeping the \"Linga\" is not open for \"beef eaters\" (non Hindu or non Buddhist or tourist). Behind this temple is the Bagumati river. Beyond the river on a hill there are many more temple structures mixed with lot of huge trees. Those areas are accessible for tourist. Now the ticket is 1000 Nepali rupees per person. \nPashupatinath is a World Heritage site. Undoubtedly it is one of the pride of Nepal Nation.",
        "review_tip": null,
